## 🧠 Software Processes

**Fundamental Activities:**
- Specification – defining what the system should do
- Design & Implementation – organizing and building the system
- Validation – checking it does what the customer wants
- Evolution – changing the system as needs change

**Process Models:**
- Waterfall – sequential phases, best for stable requirements
- Incremental Development – interleaved activities, rapid feedback
- Reuse-Oriented Engineering – integrating existing components
- Spiral Model – risk-driven, iterative
- Rational Unified Process (RUP) – combines waterfall, incremental, and spiral

**Coping with Change:**
- Prototyping – early version to test concepts
- Incremental Delivery – deliver high-priority features first

