## 🔄 Agile Development & XP

**Agile Principles:**
- Customer Involvement – close collaboration throughout
- Incremental Delivery – frequent releases
- People, Not Process – trust the team
- Embrace Change – expect and adapt to changes
- Maintain Simplicity – eliminate complexity

**Extreme Programming (XP) Practices:**
- Pair Programming – two devs, one screen
- Test-First Development – write tests before code
- Continuous Integration – integrate and test daily
- Refactoring – continuously improve code
- Collective Ownership – anyone can change anything
- Small Releases – ship minimal useful features first
- On-Site Customer – customer available full-time

**Agile vs Plan-Driven:**
| Aspect            | Agile                      | Plan-Driven              |
|-------------------|----------------------------|--------------------------|
| Planning          | Incremental                | Upfront, detailed        |
| Documentation     | Minimal                    | Extensive                |
| Requirements      | Evolve over time           | Fixed early              |
| Best for          | Small teams, dynamic needs | Large/regulated systems  |

**Scaling Agile:**
- Large systems need more upfront design
- Cross-team communication is critical
- Continuous integration becomes harder but still valuable

