## ✅ Software Quality Assurance (SQA)

**Definition:**
SQA is a set of activities that ensure processes, procedures, and standards are suitable for the project and correctly implemented. It works **in parallel** with development.

**Elements of SQA:**
- Standards (IEEE, ISO)
- Reviews & Audits
- Testing (planned and efficient)
- Error/Defect Analysis
- Change Management
- Education & Training
- Security Management
- Safety & Risk Management

**Focus Areas:**
- Portability – adapt to different environments
- Usability – intuitive and easy to use
- Reusability – components can be reused
- Correctness – meets requirements
- Maintainability – easy to modify/extend
- Error Control – handle and recover from failures

**Benefits:**
- Produces high-quality software
- Saves time and cost in the long run
- Reduces maintenance overhead
- Increases market share for commercial products

**Challenges:**
- Cost and time overhead
- Resource intensive
- Resistance from teams
- Complex to implement in large projects

